	(text "FLOW_METER_DATA has to be a PWM B pin, if you want to use \nthe PWM to measure frequency. If so, the A pin should \nnot be used for PWM. GP23 is a B pin."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 119.888 166.116 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "0250f32a-94e8-478d-a469-c8ba3295ed0d")
	)
	(text "An RC filter helps reduce high frequecy noise\nwhich may couple into the traces. 47 ohm/4.7 µF\nwas selected due to it being common components\nand give a reasonable cut-off frequency."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 208.28 84.582 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "02e837a2-a92d-4ffa-9d4e-4bb60493e6ed")
	)
	(text "PWM9A"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 121.92 146.558 90)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "03aad006-8478-4493-825f-0488cff30aa5")
	)
	(text "Do you need this boost converter? No. If you're designing a dev\nboard, it can however be nice to get a \"correct\" VIN voltage.\nThat way you get full ADC performance."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 302.26 249.428 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "1a532de9-9e4e-41e4-8764-1b7270c4ddf5")
	)
	(text "Pin order is \nimportant here \nto be able to \nuse PIO for SDIO."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 133.604 25.4 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "2c459cb7-c5c7-46f3-8a83-f2b44cc33d5f")
	)
	(text "This is part of the reference design from TI. The values for the\nfilter and the reference resistor should be selected to match the\nexcitation current and filter frequence (330 Hz).\n\nFor a 4 lead RTD (SBAA336b) or 2 lead RTD (SBAA329b): \nR_Ref = 1.62K\nR = 3.16K\nC = 100 nF\n\nFor a 3 lead RTD with two IDAC current sources (SBAA330c):\nR_Ref = 820R\nR = 4.02K\nC = 100 nF"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 220.98 137.668 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "2e4247e9-97d4-4d7d-a647-23ba325064cf")
	)
	(text "12V 5W Power Supply"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 420.624 601.472 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "3bb54cb9-22af-4824-974e-2b633ea67d52")
	)
	(text "This is basically just the reference design \nfrom TI. This filter should be frequency \nmatched (330 Hz) to the filter the reference resistor)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 1037.844 684.53 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "45eb3f41-4fa7-4681-b1ea-83b51cbe8234")
	)
	(text "82/10 gives us 11.5 V output."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 285.242 289.56 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "4703763c-ab66-425c-bf24-32cf94ef53af")
	)
	(text "An RC filter helps reduce high frequecy noise\nwhich may couple into the cables. 47 ohm/4.7 µF\nwas selected due to it being common components\nand give a reasonable cut-off frequency."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
